{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120603","id":3927063432,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7qEjuI","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120603","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120603.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120603.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120603","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120603/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120603/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120603/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2448996f8a6b3d21e8a586cbc15a40bcf0bc6183","number":120603,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Vulkan: Don't let VMA enforce maxMemoryAllocationCount","user":{"login":"vorvek","id":9655848,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTU4NDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9655848?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek","html_url":"https://github.com/vorvek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vorvek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Bug\r\n\r\nGodot 4.7 crashes on load in Forward+/Mobile (Vulkan) on AMD **integrated** GPUs (Ryzen APUs / \"AMD Radeon Graphics\") for content-heavy projects, with a flood of `VkResult error -10` on `buffer_create` / `texture_create`. `-10` is `VK_ERROR_TOO_MANY_OBJECTS`. Regression from 4.6; does not affect NVIDIA, AMD discrete, or D3D12. Fixes #120534.\r\n\r\n## Root cause\r\n\r\nThe 4.7 VMA update (3.1.0 to 3.3.0, 805c9d4b18) pulled in upstream VMA commit [`89d3a6a`](https://github.com/GPUOpen-LibrariesAndSDKs/VulkanMemoryAllocator/commit/89d3a6a5ea35d140fe865ed493c89bde777c6a07), which **changed the default of `VMA_DEBUG_DONT_EXCEED_MAX_MEMORY_ALLOCATION_COUNT` from `0` to `1`**. With it on, VMA returns `VK_ERROR_TOO_MANY_OBJECTS` itself the moment the live `VkDeviceMemory` count reaches `maxMemoryAllocationCount`, instead of forwarding the allocation to the driver:\r\n\r\n```c\r\n#if VMA_DEBUG_DONT_EXCEED_MAX_MEMORY_ALLOCATION_COUNT\r\n    if (prevDeviceMemoryCount >= m_PhysicalDeviceProperties.limits.maxMemoryAllocationCount)\r\n        return VK_ERROR_TOO_MANY_OBJECTS;\r\n#endif\r\n```\r\n\r\nAMD iGPUs report a low `maxMemoryAllocationCount` (typically 4096); content-heavy projects cross it during load. On 4.6 (VMA 3.1.0, macro `= 0`) VMA forwarded these and the driver serviced them; on 4.7 it refuses them, so resource creation fails and the project crashes. This is **not** a Godot-side leak; RenderingDevice RID counts stay flat and small (verified with a probe build), and the renderer already made >4096 distinct allocations on these GPUs before 4.7, which the driver tolerated.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\nDefine the macro back to `0` in `vk_mem_alloc.cpp`. One line, keeps the rest of the 3.3.0 update.\r\n\r\n## Possible follow-up\r\n\r\nThis restores 4.6 behavior, which relies on the driver accepting more than the reported limit. The spec-clean follow-up is to reduce the *number* of distinct device allocations on low-limit GPUs (larger sub-allocated blocks for small buffers/images); that is a bigger change than this regression warrants.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\nReporter confirmed a VMA-reverted build no longer crashes; a build with only this one-line change is linked from the issue for confirmation.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":205417413,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDU0MTc0MTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:windows","name":"platform:windows","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471795,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE3OTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:thirdparty","name":"topic:thirdparty","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1332303119,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzMyMzAzMTE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/regression","name":"regression","description":"","color":"ff63ac","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","followin